{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00413",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.79,
      "end_seconds": 2.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Morning! Make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.28,
      "end_seconds": 4.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "good afternoon"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 5.65,
      "end_seconds": 8.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.17,
      "end_seconds": 18.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here. What made you decide to come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 18.74,
      "end_seconds": 23.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Doctor, it's terrible shaking and sweating. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.02,
      "end_seconds": 27.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "when did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.85,
      "end_seconds": 31.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "It's been two weeks now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.32,
      "end_seconds": 35.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "is it mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.87,
      "end_seconds": 39.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "It feels severe to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.66,
      "end_seconds": 44.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.13,
      "end_seconds": 55.77,
      "duration_seconds": 6.64,
      "text": "when it starts I tend to get fever with chills as well"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.73,
      "end_seconds": 58.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Have you had nausea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.26,
      "end_seconds": 74.71,
      "duration_seconds": 14.45,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, ten days. The fever with chills? That's been for three days. I did have a headache at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.78,
      "end_seconds": 82.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.43,
      "text": "So, have you had terrible shaking and sweating before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.38,
      "end_seconds": 91.92,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "yes, something like this happened about six months ago, and it went away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.58,
      "end_seconds": 98.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 100.45,
      "end_seconds": 108.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "She takes Seretide inhaler, twice a day. It's Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.67,
      "end_seconds": 111.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "And for how long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 112.87,
      "end_seconds": 118.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "For about a month. She takes paracetamol, 500 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.04,
      "end_seconds": 122.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 123.57,
      "end_seconds": 124.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "For six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.38,
      "end_seconds": 129.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.8,
      "end_seconds": 145.83,
      "duration_seconds": 15.03,
      "text": "I don't drink at all. I've never smoked. Yes, I'm a nurse on a busy ward. I skip breakfast most days. Not really, I don't get much exercise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.09,
      "end_seconds": 161.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Are there any allergies on your record that I should check?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.21,
      "end_seconds": 174.84,
      "duration_seconds": 11.63,
      "text": "hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic but I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.26,
      "end_seconds": 193.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "so, any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.66,
      "end_seconds": 197.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "yes, asthma i've got diabetes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.93,
      "end_seconds": 199.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "right, any more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.85,
      "end_seconds": 208.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "Alright, diabetes, that matches what I have here. Any cough, vomiting or breathlessness at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.01,
      "end_seconds": 214.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "I haven't had cough, vomiting or breathlessness, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.25,
      "end_seconds": 218.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Any rash, diarrhoea or stiff neck at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.86,
      "end_seconds": 222.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "no, none of those"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.05,
      "end_seconds": 226.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.69,
      "end_seconds": 230.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.28,
      "end_seconds": 236.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.65,
      "end_seconds": 239.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.85,
      "end_seconds": 243.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.13,
      "end_seconds": 252.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Okay, give me a a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.72,
      "end_seconds": 274.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.8,
      "text": "okay: pulse 99, temperature 38.2, BP is 104 over 76, SpO2 95 percent on room air"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.39,
      "end_seconds": 278.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.85,
      "end_seconds": 283.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "They help build the picture, I'll tell you more soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.69,
      "end_seconds": 320.63,
      "duration_seconds": 17.94,
      "text": "so, based on your history, I'd lean towards malaria until proven otherwise another possibility is a viral illness let me just check I've got this right you've had terrible shaking and sweating for two weeks, severe, and no cough or diarrhoea"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.91,
      "end_seconds": 326.61,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.57,
      "end_seconds": 336.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "let's book blood tests to look into fever. A malaria test is what I'd like next, for fever after travel"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.27,
      "end_seconds": 340.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Alright, when would that be?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.51,
      "end_seconds": 358.66,
      "duration_seconds": 16.15,
      "text": "Let the lab know you travelled recently, that's important for the tests. A dengue test is something we might do if this doesn't improve in two weeks. Let's review you in two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.68,
      "end_seconds": 363.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Good, I'll come back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.3,
      "end_seconds": 368.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "good. Let us know how you get on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.79,
      "end_seconds": 370.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "I appreciate it, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.36,
      "end_seconds": 372.06,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Goodbye."
    }
  ]
}